values ('e0f1a2b3-4c5d-4e15-8f74-8a9b0c1d2e05', 'hospitality-law', 'Hospitality Law', 'Hospitality Law prepares future hotel, restaurant, resort, club, and event leaders to recognize and manage legal risk in the United States. Students analyze contracts and agency, innkeeper–guest duties, torts and premises liability, safety and emergencies, food and alcohol regulation, employment and labor, accessibility and civil rights, franchising and management agreements, consumer protection, intellectual property, privacy and cybersecurity, insurance, compliance, investigations, and dispute resolution. Through cases, statutes, regulations, simulations, and professional writing, students learn to identify controlling authority, apply rules to facts, preserve evidence, communicate uncertainty, and escalate matters responsibly.');

