  'Hospitality Law',
  'Hospitality Law prepares future hotel, restaurant, resort, club, and event leaders to recognize and manage legal risk in the United States. Students analyze contracts and agency, innkeeper–guest duties, torts and premises liability, safety and emergencies, food and alcohol regulation, employment and labor, accessibility and civil rights, franchising and management agreements, consumer protection, intellectual property, privacy and cybersecurity, insurance, compliance, investigations, and dispute resolution. Through cases, statutes, regulations, simulations, and professional writing, students learn to identify controlling authority, apply rules to facts, preserve evidence, communicate uncertainty, and escalate matters responsibly.',
  $hlawjson${"slug": "hospitality-law", "title": "Hospitality Law", "description": "Hospitality Law prepares future hotel, restaurant, resort, club, and event leaders to recognize and manage legal risk in the United States. Students analyze contracts and agency, innkeeper–guest duties, torts and premises liability, safety and emergencies, food and alcohol regulation, employment and labor, accessibility and civil rights, franchising and management agreements, consumer protection, intellectual property, privacy and cybersecurity, insurance, compliance, investigations, and dispute resolution. Through cases, statutes, regulations, simulations, and professional writing, students learn to identify controlling authority, apply rules to facts, preserve evidence, communicate uncertainty, and escalate matters responsibly.", "topics": [{"id": "b98462b1-1f6b-42c1-b23f-aac1d062a1cf", "type": "topic", "title": "The American Legal System and Hospitality Decision-Making", "description": "Hospitality managers operate where federal, state, tribal, territorial, and local rules overlap. This section builds the legal literacy needed to recognize an issue, find controlling authority, preserve facts, and involve qualified counsel before an operational problem becomes a claim.", "children": [{"id": "8271beca-2277-405d-ad50-d23c9f858981", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sources and hierarchy of law", "children": [{"id": "ea686003-2054-4448-aa5e-66726fda3139", "type": "concept", "title": "U.S. Constitution; federal and state constitutions"}, {"id": "bf84affe-a4ec-463c-be28-dd488d45b328", "type": "concept", "title": "Statutes, regulations, ordinances, administrative guidance, and licensing conditions"}, {"id": "179f3391-803a-43fe-8c09-63e7b2217154", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal and state judicial opinions; binding precedent versus persuasive authority"}], "description": "Students learn which legal authority controls, how conflicts are resolved, and why an online summary is not a substitute for current primary law."}, {"id": "15e233d9-2de9-4c36-998b-5c513307203d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Courts, agencies, jurisdiction, and procedure", "children": [{"id": "539fa714-b222-47b8-a211-657ad8ea9618", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal and state trial and appellate courts; subject-matter and personal jurisdiction"}, {"id": "52a766fa-c3bd-4438-81b0-f84d857e0c84", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative agencies, investigations, inspections, hearings, penalties, and judicial review"}, {"id": "bf51ed3b-8e9d-4f98-92d8-cc89d327f7f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Pleadings, discovery, motions, trial, appeals, burdens of proof, remedies, and limitation periods"}], "description": "This subtopic maps the institutions that create, enforce, and interpret hospitality obligations."}, {"id": "6f3a04b4-5897-45f3-b85f-fecedeb1274c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Managerial issue spotting and escalation", "children": [{"id": "56b37582-e457-4a1f-92c6-5af700152070", "type": "concept", "title": "Parties, duties, conduct, causation, injury, defenses, damages, and available remedies"}, {"id": "bbe599f0-b38e-4486-851b-371d325e0c04", "type": "concept", "title": "Privilege, litigation holds, records preservation, incident reports, and communications discipline"}, {"id": "42fd5f2b-5e58-4159-914d-a846f8e9249e", "type": "concept", "title": "Counsel referral, insurer notice, regulator response, expert consultation, and decision documentation"}], "description": "Students practice turning an operational story into legally relevant facts, questions, evidence, and decisions without pretending to provide legal advice."}]}, {"id": "30bfa9b3-db9e-423b-a01d-e489ee9267c1", "type": "topic", "title": "Contracts, Agency, and Commercial Commitments", "description": "Hospitality operations are built on promises to guests, groups, suppliers, owners, brands, platforms, and employees. Students learn how agreements form, who may bind the enterprise, and how contract language allocates operational and financial risk.", "children": [{"id": "8c73ef71-a2ab-4d9c-ad3e-4ada85ea46ad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Formation, interpretation, and enforceability", "children": [{"id": "c280d2e8-48fe-4007-85f3-18c12d4742f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Offer, acceptance, consideration, mutual assent, capacity, legality, and definite terms"}, {"id": "c5064a15-8c29-4c99-84a4-a0c3cc534048", "type": "concept", "title": "Written, oral, electronic, clickwrap, course-of-dealing, and implied agreements"}, {"id": "bbc61f6a-a34b-447e-8da8-4857c23a9b13", "type": "concept", "title": "Statute of Frauds, parol evidence, ambiguity, modification, waiver, severability, and electronic signatures"}], "description": "Students learn the elements of a contract and the recurring defects that make an apparent promise uncertain or unenforceable."}, {"id": "8715bfad-d1fe-46f6-920d-bf8c0288232e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance, breach, defenses, and remedies", "children": [{"id": "1f6e43e6-73ad-4a49-a6d0-434a24236f34", "type": "concept", "title": "Conditions, covenants, representations, warranties, standards, milestones, and acceptance"}, {"id": "c3cf1b13-33f2-4df9-8cac-f458ff54ad75", "type": "concept", "title": "Material breach, anticipatory repudiation, impossibility, impracticability, frustration, mistake, duress, and unconscionability"}, {"id": "752950be-af47-454b-9b23-87935d64eb09", "type": "concept", "title": "Expectation, reliance, restitution, liquidated damages, mitigation, specific performance, termination, and cure"}], "description": "This subtopic connects contract doctrine to cancellations, service failures, payment disputes, and disrupted events."}, {"id": "9dbf02b0-124d-49f6-bae6-20ae3ecf86cf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Agency and authority", "children": [{"id": "1e3b99e3-7830-4c2c-9c89-6e3abca49e76", "type": "concept", "title": "Actual, implied, apparent, and ratified authority"}, {"id": "41798752-1f2e-4c27-ad2f-cc4bf4bf09ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Principal and agent duties; disclosed, partially disclosed, and undisclosed principals"}, {"id": "851d055e-0e6e-4666-afcf-a61d5aae1ca1", "type": "concept", "title": "Vicarious liability, independent contractors, scope of employment, and authority controls"}], "description": "Students examine when employees, managers, agents, travel sellers, and platforms create obligations for another party."}]}, {"id": "b3d97d1f-13a6-4591-b075-f89afc76f5cd", "type": "topic", "title": "Innkeeper–Guest Relationship, Reservations, and Guest Property", "description": "Lodging law combines common-law duties, state innkeeper statutes, contracts, civil-rights rules, and consumer protections. Students learn how legal status changes from inquiry and reservation through occupancy, removal, departure, and lost-property handling.", "children": [{"id": "bbcc3975-a826-4075-846f-d65342aeebde", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Admission, reservations, rates, and nondiscrimination", "children": [{"id": "003fdbbd-d338-4acb-bda0-fe4942c8cbca", "type": "concept", "title": "Guest status, right to exclude, lawful refusal, protected classes, and neutral conduct rules"}, {"id": "7d0841d6-ec67-4e7d-93e2-40be19de67f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Reservation confirmation, deposits, guarantees, cancellations, no-shows, overbooking, and walking guests"}, {"id": "2f697650-428c-4794-8516-452b767f71af", "type": "concept", "title": "Rate disclosure, mandatory fees, taxes, authorization holds, refunds, and records"}], "description": "Students evaluate when a lodging operator may refuse service, what reservation promises mean, and how published terms must align with public-accommodation duties."}, {"id": "a9ba849a-4acb-4b18-aac1-c537604e74e4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Occupancy, privacy, access, and removal", "children": [{"id": "b9e49176-2c83-4ae3-ad9a-4e5555d53d07", "type": "concept", "title": "Guest privacy, room entry, housekeeping, maintenance, emergencies, warrants, subpoenas, and law-enforcement requests"}, {"id": "ed8a237c-21ec-4cc6-8c3c-702017735acd", "type": "concept", "title": "Distinguishing guest, tenant, licensee, trespasser, and long-term occupant under state law"}, {"id": "ad108c33-bffd-411d-a6ab-8f2d6bc4c2c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Eviction or ejection, breach of peace, abandoned rooms, safe procedures, and counsel/law-enforcement escalation"}], "description": "This subtopic addresses the guest's possessory and privacy interests and the operator's safety and property-management responsibilities."}, {"id": "97e8175d-2180-4ae0-a605-5dd40cedc17b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bailment, safekeeping, lost property, and statutory limits", "children": [{"id": "25d8fba6-aca0-4848-aa72-c425fa9257e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Bailment formation, standard of care, proof, defenses, and damages"}, {"id": "68bc96a6-55ca-4413-ba07-8cee8282682b", "type": "concept", "title": "Innkeeper statutes, safe-deposit procedures, posted notices, parking disclaimers, and limits of liability"}, {"id": "7e7d9747-f7d6-4275-be3b-7cdf4c50075d", "type": "concept", "title": "Lost-and-found chain of custody, retention, disposal, employee property, and evidence preservation"}], "description": "Students learn how custody and notice affect responsibility for luggage, vehicles, valuables, and property left behind."}]}, {"id": "43eaa9a2-8b47-4561-97ff-16ec3e99d148", "type": "topic", "title": "Torts, Negligence, and Premises Liability", "description": "Hospitality businesses invite the public into spaces containing foreseeable service, crowd, pool, elevator, food, alcohol, and security risks. This section teaches a disciplined negligence analysis and the operational evidence needed to prevent or defend claims.", "children": [{"id": "c0bd69e1-ddcb-4184-9db3-630151d0d647", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intentional torts and business responsibility", "children": [{"id": "a4355494-5ba7-4da4-8c59-3e12880d7378", "type": "concept", "title": "Assault, battery, false imprisonment, trespass, conversion, defamation, privacy torts, and intentional infliction"}, {"id": "0ab82a45-a0d4-4e34-9bf7-ed23eb362693", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, privilege, self-defense, defense of others or property, merchant detention, and use of force"}, {"id": "9929109c-b569-4c37-a856-b60b111b6aed", "type": "concept", "title": "Respondeat superior, negligent hiring/supervision/retention, ratification, and punitive damages"}], "description": "Students distinguish intentional conduct from negligence and identify when an employer may be liable for employee or security actions."}, {"id": "d9f2dae7-b1f9-44c9-ba0c-d1e809e8301e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Negligence framework", "children": [{"id": "ca09139e-9463-4055-9830-019f578724d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Reasonable care, industry custom, statutes and negligence per se, professional standards, and foreseeable plaintiffs"}, {"id": "76264dae-edd6-44d5-bf6b-599a6791949a", "type": "concept", "title": "Actual and proximate causation, intervening acts, multiple causes, and proof"}, {"id": "fb958941-89c9-43b5-97bb-676e0cf07e07", "type": "concept", "title": "Compensatory damages, comparative or contributory fault, assumption of risk, waivers, and indemnity"}], "description": "This subtopic builds the core method for analyzing duty, breach, causation, injury, and defenses."}, {"id": "8f7062f8-37af-46ca-b6f6-be7283c62c4c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Premises, products, and third-party acts", "children": [{"id": "3458fbd1-a2da-49f9-bdae-b0707052b27e", "type": "concept", "title": "Inspection, notice, maintenance, warnings, lighting, flooring, stairs, balconies, pools, spas, elevators, and parking"}, {"id": "0caf9b94-fa4a-40c2-88e1-a44712727685", "type": "concept", "title": "Invitees, licensees, trespassers, children, recreational activities, and jurisdictional variations"}, {"id": "c3d8bc19-9d40-4783-a505-2fb8b979c8cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreseeable crime, security plans, keys and locks, vendors, products liability, recalls, and evidence"}], "description": "Students apply negligence doctrine to physical conditions, products, vendors, criminal acts, and changing property use."}]}, {"id": "e93a57c0-6677-47e0-bf8a-cfbb5f8b24a2", "type": "topic", "title": "Safety, Security, Emergencies, and Public-Health Duties", "description": "Hospitality managers must make rapid decisions during fires, severe weather, violence, medical events, outbreaks, evacuations, and technology outages. This section connects duty of care to preparedness, response, continuity, documentation, and respectful communication.", "children": [{"id": "15ed900b-8310-4670-9c5a-3b315b6f64a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Emergency planning and duty of care", "children": [{"id": "35767f7c-1d81-4bde-9a36-27f5be4c30ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Hazard assessment, emergency action plans, evacuation, shelter, accountability, reunification, and continuity"}, {"id": "d8b5b3b2-ccae-4f66-b52f-58d84f58c6e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Fire and life safety, occupancy, alarms, suppression, exits, crowd management, pools, and transportation"}, {"id": "18765760-88f7-41dd-9ece-ed30f4c0c667", "type": "concept", "title": "Emergency roles, incident command, drills, mutual aid, contractors, and accessible communications"}], "description": "Students learn to design a proportionate all-hazards program and understand that plans must align with local codes and public-safety authorities."}, {"id": "f2c2577b-a6f5-4c7b-8c7b-7362d75ee247", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Security, violence, and safeguarding", "children": [{"id": "87b83b39-1d91-42fe-baac-e450846d5cf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Threat assessment, access control, keys, surveillance, patrol, cash, cyber-physical security, and suspicious activity"}, {"id": "b1aeaec7-2585-48c9-9dec-6234b0c7bd0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Workplace violence, trafficking indicators, vulnerable guests, minors, harassment, and escalation protocols"}, {"id": "48c9ffbb-0b14-4a26-87c2-1ef088b6558f", "type": "concept", "title": "Security contractors, off-duty police, use of force, privacy, records, and post-incident care"}], "description": "This subtopic examines reasonable protective measures without assuming that every adverse event is preventable."}, {"id": "8f08e384-780b-4ebf-9750-c904d00e73fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Medical events, outbreaks, and government orders", "children": [{"id": "0ac77327-46fd-4889-92c2-4815a7426dda", "type": "concept", "title": "First aid/AED programs, emergency medical services, Good Samaritan variation, and documentation"}, {"id": "c7723342-afbb-4dcc-a2a0-27056b479317", "type": "concept", "title": "Communicable disease, exposure, isolation, sanitation, closures, public-health orders, and worker protections"}, {"id": "b9ca7d8a-affc-4c43-98b8-200bfdb0708b", "type": "concept", "title": "Americans with Disabilities Act issues, confidentiality, rumor control, media response, and recovery"}], "description": "Students practice coordinating guest care, employee safety, operations, privacy, and agency direction during health events."}]}, {"id": "3fa82243-5fa0-462c-a233-bb1fbfa95326", "type": "topic", "title": "Food Safety, Allergens, and Alcohol Regulation", "description": "Restaurants, bars, banquets, and lodging outlets face layered state and local licensing, food-code, alcohol, and tort obligations. Students learn to translate regulatory duties into preventive controls and defensible records.", "children": [{"id": "047cca9a-4e87-4f95-bbce-003556e9a419", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Retail food regulation and active managerial control", "children": [{"id": "e58a4bb8-9683-4c38-919a-74daab13a26e", "type": "concept", "title": "Food establishment permits, inspections, grades, embargo, correction, closure, hearings, and appeals"}, {"id": "cc66cf36-5ae8-43ac-a81f-139430b6701b", "type": "concept", "title": "Person in charge, employee health, hygiene, time/temperature control, contamination, sanitation, HACCP, and variances"}, {"id": "6801fc20-68fa-4248-b453-382ad5f3ba81", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier approval, traceability, recalls, complaints, outbreak cooperation, logs, and corrective action"}], "description": "Students learn how the FDA Food Code functions as a model and why the adopted state or local code and permit conditions control the operation."}, {"id": "9cf1cf7a-18cb-4bef-83ec-c4364c255904", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food allergens and consumer communication", "children": [{"id": "17dfba8d-844c-4f3a-b0e1-b4738aa72265", "type": "concept", "title": "Nine major allergens under federal packaged-food law; jurisdiction-specific restaurant requirements"}, {"id": "e6a2b4d2-70e7-4047-8b14-151693154e27", "type": "concept", "title": "Written allergen notification under jurisdictions adopting relevant FDA Food Code provisions"}, {"id": "08a4e6f3-9009-4b9b-b269-62b8e0166144", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-contact prevention, recipe control, substitutions, server escalation, emergency response, and documentation"}], "description": "This subtopic addresses the legal and operational consequences of inaccurate ingredient, menu, and service communication."}, {"id": "32bbd449-13a0-4d8d-9b6a-7d3c5d4c8cb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Alcohol licensing and liability", "children": [{"id": "8f2e97f6-96f1-4672-85f8-f71419e93b9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Licenses, permits, tied-house and supplier issues, hours, age verification, records, and enforcement"}, {"id": "1e2aed1a-9a6c-4181-9b12-2474a2617986", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsible service, intoxication, underage service, promotions, delivery, cannabis interactions, and refusal"}, {"id": "cb1bceb3-f1a6-412f-ae01-11191c1c1862", "type": "concept", "title": "Dram-shop and social-host liability, causation, safe transportation, incident reporting, and insurance"}], "description": "Students compare the three-tier system and state/local rules while recognizing that service, age, hours, promotions, and liability vary substantially by jurisdiction."}]}, {"id": "6ff36760-bd3b-410d-b2d8-cabc181e62ed", "type": "topic", "title": "Employment, Wage-and-Hour, Labor, and Immigration Compliance", "description": "Hospitality's round-the-clock, tipped, multilingual, seasonal, and franchise-based workforce creates distinctive legal risk. This section helps future managers apply fair, documented practices and recognize when federal, state, local, union, or immigration rules require specialist support.", "children": [{"id": "ca731f04-99e0-41f5-9d03-3de4dd68df79", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wage-and-hour and scheduling", "children": [{"id": "6014f98e-04df-49f6-a0c6-3c709adbbbf1", "type": "concept", "title": "FLSA coverage, employee versus contractor, exempt versus nonexempt, hours worked, regular rate, overtime, and records"}, {"id": "2750b638-7e8e-4279-b8a9-481b9d958906", "type": "concept", "title": "Tip credit, notice, tip pools, managers and tips, service charges, dual jobs, shortages, uniforms, and lodging/meal credits"}, {"id": "b72b6d63-9051-4b32-aaf4-1771da897f60", "type": "concept", "title": "State/local minimum wages, predictive scheduling, meal/rest periods, pay frequency, final pay, expense reimbursement, and paid leave"}], "description": "Students examine the records and classification decisions behind wages, tips, overtime, deductions, meals, uniforms, and working time."}, {"id": "83354034-6257-4892-aa44-3a3b3c0fae22", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equal employment opportunity and accommodation", "children": [{"id": "4c2fcb7a-a3e6-4bd1-b4d2-82ba42f6f2b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Title VII, ADA, ADEA, Equal Pay Act, GINA, Pregnancy Workers Fairness Act, and state/local protections"}, {"id": "6e31849c-da28-431f-bd17-48bb196b3531", "type": "concept", "title": "Disability, religion, pregnancy, lactation, interactive process, undue hardship, confidentiality, and retaliation"}, {"id": "a035349a-9ba1-426a-b40f-1aa341f1584f", "type": "concept", "title": "Harassment by supervisors, coworkers, guests, vendors, and digital channels; reporting, investigation, and corrective action"}], "description": "This subtopic covers nondiscrimination across recruitment, assignment, pay, promotion, discipline, harassment prevention, accommodation, and separation."}, {"id": "832c2251-4f00-4b1a-a932-8cc31401b731", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Labor relations, leave, safety, and work authorization", "children": [{"id": "c6446d4c-2ae8-40e5-9c89-caf2f7cb077b", "type": "concept", "title": "NLRA protected concerted activity, wage discussions, organizing, supervisors, union rules, bargaining, and discipline"}, {"id": "af0adace-7ab5-4d6c-8fc2-069c7bff6b10", "type": "concept", "title": "OSHA duties, hazard communication, injury records, workers' compensation, FMLA, USERRA, and state leave laws"}, {"id": "0353ae7c-eca1-49e8-a266-d29e400b9477", "type": "concept", "title": "Form I-9, nondiscriminatory verification, E-Verify where applicable, visas, minors, trafficking risks, and document retention"}], "description": "Students learn the overlapping rights that affect employee voice, injury prevention, leave, organizing, and verification."}]}, {"id": "4e02811c-dbb9-42cc-b27d-9aab10d09df5", "type": "topic", "title": "Accessibility and Civil Rights in Guest Service", "description": "American hospitality is a public-accommodation setting. Students learn to design equal access across reservations, facilities, transportation, digital channels, communication, policies, and emergency procedures—not merely react to complaints.", "children": [{"id": "fa9b3d53-eabe-4ca6-909d-50b3b5a0cab1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ADA Title III service obligations", "children": [{"id": "6f1cc06a-451e-43e5-a863-4bf8a616ac6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Public accommodations, eligibility criteria, surcharges, direct threat, fundamental alteration, and undue burden"}, {"id": "952ed21b-95a2-4796-9ce5-824deb01f04e", "type": "concept", "title": "Service animals, mobility devices, auxiliary aids, interpreters, captioning, accessible formats, and companions"}, {"id": "449f907b-f6ff-4406-b25a-c1372bccaa13", "type": "concept", "title": "Reservation staff knowledge, accessible-room information, room holds, equivalent options, and training"}], "description": "Students apply the concepts of equal enjoyment, reasonable policy modification, effective communication, and barrier removal to real hospitality interactions."}, {"id": "cb7ee80f-1274-4098-b8f4-f15bfcf1b976", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Facilities, alterations, and operational access", "children": [{"id": "980df0ba-90b5-4d83-aafa-c37afbdd16a8", "type": "concept", "title": "2010 ADA Standards, new construction, alterations, path of travel, barrier removal, and readily achievable analysis"}, {"id": "f899dd81-07c9-4242-955b-d1629eb618b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Entrances, parking, counters, guest rooms, bathrooms, pools, restaurants, meeting rooms, fitness, transportation, and evacuation"}, {"id": "2801f129-856c-46d3-900e-a275f17c0592", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance of accessible features, temporary barriers, furniture, snow, outages, inspections, and remediation"}], "description": "This subtopic links design standards with daily practices that keep accessible features usable."}, {"id": "aca43de3-99be-45f6-be02-7cd5247ed980", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital access and broader civil-rights duties", "children": [{"id": "852e46e3-c565-4be2-a91c-bbbd9fbb3aff", "type": "concept", "title": "Booking, menus, check-in, digital keys, loyalty, employment portals, documents, and effective alternatives"}, {"id": "a3fe1bd4-3a54-4129-97fc-7132f4832dbf", "type": "concept", "title": "DOJ web-accessibility guidance, WCAG as a technical reference, procurement, testing, complaints, and remediation"}, {"id": "5e14bb65-1eb8-4684-89ae-d7f0a11cf077", "type": "concept", "title": "Race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, and other state/local protected classes"}], "description": "Students examine websites, apps, kiosks, and the interaction of federal law with state and local public-accommodation protections."}]}, {"id": "4656b6b5-1367-43ed-8b30-3b1b2d6e494c", "type": "topic", "title": "Ownership, Franchising, Management Agreements, and Real Estate", "description": "Hospitality assets often separate ownership, brand, operation, employment, real estate, and intellectual property. This section helps students identify who controls which decision and where obligations, fees, standards, and liability reside.", "children": [{"id": "4e63b7fc-61fb-4368-ac7c-f39e2729828c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Entity, ownership, and authority structures", "children": [{"id": "59567bdb-d64a-41f0-a108-9459424b5daf", "type": "concept", "title": "Corporations, limited liability companies, partnerships, joint ventures, owners, operators, brands, and asset managers"}, {"id": "5cc0b336-b258-4909-acfa-df364952cb47", "type": "concept", "title": "Governing documents, fiduciary duties, authority matrices, guarantees, indemnities, and intercompany agreements"}, {"id": "9690d7d1-b8b2-4067-9bb0-ba3707c333e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Bankruptcy, receivership, lender rights, change of control, due diligence, and successor exposure"}], "description": "Students map legal entities and decision rights before attributing a promise, duty, asset, employee, or claim to the wrong party."}, {"id": "2ea33f7c-f1be-48ee-973e-fa9c2692c00f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Franchise relationships", "children": [{"id": "e267a8a9-a871-41c7-b163-e5d2b0feb421", "type": "concept", "title": "FTC Franchise Rule, Franchise Disclosure Document, 23 disclosure items, timing, and earnings claims"}, {"id": "a13d6835-e72c-4675-8810-22588f5b577a", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand standards, fees, reservations, loyalty, procurement, technology, territory, quality assurance, defaults, cure, and termination"}, {"id": "67ba5c9b-580f-44ac-b687-0ff520a90a39", "type": "concept", "title": "State registration and relationship laws, encroachment, good faith, vicarious liability, and joint-employer concerns"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces federal disclosure rules and the contract and state-law issues that shape hotel and restaurant franchises."}, {"id": "9fe1925a-de78-4232-bf84-117b6176eca5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hotel management and property agreements", "children": [{"id": "ede4fbc7-bde5-4445-8a46-614c525400c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Owner/operator roles, term, base and incentive fees, budget, personnel, accounts, procurement, and performance tests"}, {"id": "010301a9-66c6-4e08-be64-e790d184836c", "type": "concept", "title": "Licenses, leases, easements, zoning, permits, land use, environmental conditions, and nuisance"}, {"id": "3a781cc6-a334-4771-81f6-5811654f4deb", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital plans, insurance, indemnity, condemnation, casualty, force majeure, termination, and transition"}], "description": "Students compare management contracts and real-estate arrangements that determine control, economics, standards, and exit rights."}]}, {"id": "a2a659df-7e31-4fce-afa6-929a99b6bd91", "type": "topic", "title": "Consumer Protection, Marketing, Pricing, and Intellectual Property", "description": "Hospitality representations appear in rates, fees, menus, reviews, loyalty terms, photos, music, events, and influencer content. Students learn to assess what a reasonable consumer is likely to understand and whether the business can substantiate its claims and rights.", "children": [{"id": "7f921f53-d792-448e-b746-b44b59a6642e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pricing, fees, promotions, and unfair practices", "children": [{"id": "c5c457b7-f09d-45a6-be59-359ba15bd616", "type": "concept", "title": "Total price disclosure for covered short-term lodging, mandatory fees, optional add-ons, taxes, clear and conspicuous presentation"}, {"id": "9f49a848-91ae-437d-8a4f-b2893cbc2615", "type": "concept", "title": "Coupons, packages, deposits, refunds, cancellation, scarcity claims, loyalty prices, gift cards, and automatic renewal"}, {"id": "091d2669-dedb-4e4e-a090-e53817d69da1", "type": "concept", "title": "Unfair or deceptive acts, state UDAP laws, attorney-general enforcement, private claims, class actions, and records"}], "description": "Students connect the FTC Act, the federal rule on unfair or deceptive fees, and state consumer-protection law to the guest purchase journey."}, {"id": "23f41b5f-aa0c-4c11-9666-ac560b397a2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advertising, reviews, and endorsements", "children": [{"id": "ab66e8d2-a7bb-4886-a34c-f1a7fbcd2227", "type": "concept", "title": "Claim substantiation, disclosures, photos, amenities, accessibility, sustainability, health, safety, and comparative claims"}, {"id": "a3c5b487-7b0c-4af2-b965-0a3f6c9cbb5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Influencers, employees, affiliates, travel advisors, native advertising, endorsements, and material connections"}, {"id": "a072d141-2a52-4a3d-94c2-2b9278044d53", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer reviews, fake reviews, suppression, incentives, platform terms, reputation management, and defamation risk"}], "description": "This subtopic focuses on truthful claims, material connections, review integrity, and consistency across direct and intermediary channels."}, {"id": "bedba8c0-dd76-44b9-a82d-3783adcc1837", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intellectual property and publicity", "children": [{"id": "0ca3f8e9-6776-4423-9dea-ace30c0920c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Trademarks, trade dress, domain names, licenses, franchised marks, quality control, and infringement"}, {"id": "4c3b9aac-7697-4331-befc-6aebaefe8d2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Copyright in photos, menus, websites, software, music, video, décor, training, and user-generated content"}, {"id": "16e407b8-de15-43b8-aa9d-64f3268f86ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Patents, trade secrets, confidentiality, employee work, rights of publicity, releases, and takedowns"}], "description": "Students identify the permissions needed to use brands, creative works, performances, guest images, and event content."}]}, {"id": "7ab33aaa-3d8d-498f-926b-5e188a270132", "type": "topic", "title": "Privacy, Data Security, Surveillance, and Technology Law", "description": "Hospitality businesses collect identity, payment, location, preference, loyalty, employment, and sometimes biometric data. Students learn to map the data life cycle, honor representations, reduce unnecessary collection, and prepare for incidents across a patchwork of U.S. laws.", "children": [{"id": "2ef4cd43-5c5d-41f7-90b0-efb88cac6fab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Privacy governance and consumer rights", "children": [{"id": "35b0a4a9-ec19-4468-b658-6a1a9ab6d44d", "type": "concept", "title": "Data inventory, classification, purpose, minimization, notice, consent, access, correction, deletion, retention, disposal, and accountability"}, {"id": "7768125b-89dd-4a78-985f-7cf1295fd2d7", "type": "concept", "title": "State comprehensive privacy laws, biometric and facial-recognition laws, children's data, marketing communications, cookies, and location"}, {"id": "2005714d-98f1-425d-b5e6-e6f59650ef1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Service providers, data sales/sharing, cross-border transfers, loyalty programs, sensitive data, and dark patterns"}], "description": "Students examine what data is collected, why, under which notice or permission, and which jurisdiction or contract governs it."}, {"id": "4e411651-7907-4e18-af6c-3d5a70523fd7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reasonable security and vendor risk", "children": [{"id": "9180786d-0431-4340-ab8b-0153567ecc91", "type": "concept", "title": "FTC Act, state security statutes, PCI DSS as a contractual standard, incident representations, and industry practice"}, {"id": "ab67c825-d5a0-469c-9843-4f6e95f085a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Access control, multifactor authentication, encryption, patching, logging, backups, physical security, training, and testing"}, {"id": "bcee648b-f1d0-44d1-8e40-a283f57433b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Cloud, PMS/POS, franchise, platform, payment, Wi-Fi, IoT, vendor diligence, security clauses, audit, and termination"}], "description": "This subtopic translates legal expectations and contractual duties into governance and operational safeguards."}, {"id": "0231897d-50b8-4e9c-b9d3-009dad50f1f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Surveillance, incident response, and breach notice", "children": [{"id": "a51e4c08-22dd-43fc-89e6-0ad19102b493", "type": "concept", "title": "Cameras, audio, key logs, Wi-Fi analytics, location, biometrics, employee monitoring, notices, and restricted areas"}, {"id": "8f17f9d5-0b45-4d20-9760-e67b9d3c1848", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident triage, containment, privilege, forensics, insurer, law enforcement, regulators, payment brands, and communications"}, {"id": "bb0deaa9-01ca-4ca5-bd24-515462eb7f1b", "type": "concept", "title": "State breach-notification triggers, timing, affected individuals, content, regulator/consumer-reporting notices, remediation, and lessons"}], "description": "Students balance safety and analytics with privacy, labor, discrimination, and evidence concerns."}]}, {"id": "dcb40b03-3abb-47f8-ac6d-52f37475c651", "type": "topic", "title": "Risk Management, Insurance, Indemnity, and Claims", "description": "Legal risk cannot be eliminated, but it can be allocated, financed, monitored, and reduced. This section connects contracts and insurance with operational controls, reporting discipline, and fair treatment of injured or affected people.", "children": [{"id": "0889a7ed-73ff-4ce3-8706-baed82076977", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Enterprise and operational risk assessment", "children": [{"id": "5b2ff728-c097-40c8-a49f-230f576fa662", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk registers, frequency, severity, velocity, aggregation, emerging risk, and risk appetite"}, {"id": "5895fc53-4f1c-4064-801b-e787e99324e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoid, reduce, transfer, finance, accept, monitor, and escalate"}, {"id": "7e6a1816-2d49-4726-9805-b9a6463ce63b", "type": "concept", "title": "Policies, training, inspections, maintenance, audits, complaints, near misses, corrective action, and board reporting"}], "description": "Students use a repeatable process to identify hazards, affected parties, controls, owners, evidence, and residual risk."}, {"id": "d86d0cef-b507-48f5-aee2-5540425cea92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Insurance and contractual allocation", "children": [{"id": "09c260b5-e6ec-43f2-8f95-924351a706a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Commercial general liability, property, business interruption, cyber, crime, auto, liquor, employment practices, workers' compensation, and umbrella"}, {"id": "235ef4e8-ed3f-43db-b805-e3ac0ff41b09", "type": "concept", "title": "Named insured, additional insured, occurrence, claims-made, limits, retentions, deductibles, exclusions, endorsements, and certificates"}, {"id": "25f6b966-4ab8-4b8f-b0b8-6422a3018e26", "type": "concept", "title": "Indemnity, defense, limitation of liability, waiver of subrogation, insurance requirements, and anti-indemnity variation"}], "description": "This subtopic helps managers recognize common coverage structures and contract language requiring broker or counsel review."}, {"id": "b8a6fb4e-100d-496d-b72e-ff4b983b639d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Incident, claim, and litigation readiness", "children": [{"id": "1c81d629-36a9-45c2-b4f9-04500f94f72d", "type": "concept", "title": "Immediate care, scene safety, photographs, witnesses, video retention, products, logs, and chain of custody"}, {"id": "54bf3d4e-6804-44e8-b433-1a2d14397838", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident reports, privilege, insurer notice, reservation of rights, adjusters, experts, subpoenas, and litigation holds"}, {"id": "74977cf2-6c08-489d-ac4e-9a76605ae372", "type": "concept", "title": "Root-cause analysis, remedial measures, regulator cooperation, settlement authority, and lessons learned"}], "description": "Students practice a compassionate and evidence-preserving response that avoids admissions, retaliation, spoliation, and late notice."}]}, {"id": "a4eb286f-37d7-4b41-bc12-2389acbd0930", "type": "topic", "title": "Compliance Programs, Ethics, Investigations, and Governance", "description": "A policy manual alone is not a compliance system. Students learn to build governance that assigns ownership, makes reporting safe, verifies controls, corrects problems, and connects legal duties with hospitality ethics and stakeholder trust.", "children": [{"id": "d0206957-9fbe-4cf3-a5f2-4deed9faf804", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Compliance program design", "children": [{"id": "51f61eac-077c-49f5-ad28-185570c252e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk assessment, obligations register, policies, standards, procedures, controls, owners, and evidence"}, {"id": "1251f8f3-af23-4831-b827-85ad1d8560a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Training, communications, certifications, monitoring, testing, audits, hotline, and third-party management"}, {"id": "564a4fa2-7df6-4b30-bde3-bf6b9cead052", "type": "concept", "title": "Metrics, exceptions, remediation, discipline, incentives, reporting, and continuous improvement"}], "description": "Students convert a legal inventory into practical controls and assurance activities suited to a property or enterprise."}, {"id": "42db401a-87c4-4f19-98b1-75a59b083238", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Complaints and workplace investigations", "children": [{"id": "5dad091a-c08b-4b4b-842a-0c67f9c173f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Intake, triage, conflicts, interim measures, scope, plan, witnesses, documents, interviews, and credibility"}, {"id": "c32363c5-715c-43d9-b231-badda3d640f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Need-to-know confidentiality, privilege decisions, trauma-informed practice, accommodations, translation, and records"}, {"id": "09b39104-7bcb-48ce-a89d-df39f794355e", "type": "concept", "title": "Findings, standard of proof, corrective action, communication, anti-retaliation monitoring, and appeal or review"}], "description": "This subtopic emphasizes fair, prompt, confidential-to-the-extent-possible processes that protect evidence and prohibit retaliation."}, {"id": "557128d3-528d-4e98-8c48-200d044e5c19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical judgment and governance", "children": [{"id": "989c0aca-e7ff-43b9-893f-c1601dd1820b", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicts of interest, gifts, bribery, procurement integrity, accurate books, whistleblowing, and board oversight"}, {"id": "8c9ec961-ff43-447c-ae65-c6717fea0ec2", "type": "concept", "title": "Guest dignity, worker voice, vulnerable people, environmental impacts, community relations, and human rights"}, {"id": "6c58dc44-ae32-45c1-a033-3d5a50adea60", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical frameworks, stakeholder mapping, escalation, dissent, documentation, accountability, and learning culture"}], "description": "Students analyze what responsible hospitality leadership requires when legal minimums, commercial pressure, and stakeholder interests diverge."}]}, {"id": "c1aba699-f1de-435e-90cb-674388050c83", "type": "topic", "title": "Legal Research, Case Briefing, Dispute Resolution, and Advocacy", "description": "The course culminates in the ability to read law carefully, separate rule from commentary, apply authority to facts, and communicate a defensible recommendation. Students also evaluate when negotiation, mediation, arbitration, agency process, or litigation best serves the organization and affected stakeholders.", "children": [{"id": "31d9b7e3-fae3-4c8a-bd08-7244b8e7aa6a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research and authority validation", "children": [{"id": "1bd5a79e-08b9-45b4-8dcb-58e646f559c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue statements, search terms, secondary orientation, primary authority, citators, and updating"}, {"id": "cda5a40d-718f-4990-bb23-d345f10019af", "type": "concept", "title": "Statutory and regulatory definitions, scope, exemptions, preemption, effective dates, amendments, and agency materials"}, {"id": "1ed27603-9b50-476c-8b32-dc91140f17e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal, state, tribal, territorial, and local sources; court rules; licenses; permits; contracts; and recordkeeping"}], "description": "Students learn a reproducible method for finding current law and confirming that it applies to the relevant place, date, facts, and business."}, {"id": "52796484-572b-4329-83f1-198534bff6a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case briefing and legal analysis", "children": [{"id": "9da3a3a5-a226-49bd-bca7-824ef2e14d5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Citation, court, procedural posture, legally significant facts, issue, rule, holding, reasoning, disposition, and separate opinions"}, {"id": "4a397e63-a618-45e9-b5ab-a9260abfeaca", "type": "concept", "title": "IRAC/CREAC, analogies and distinctions, counterarguments, uncertainty, policy, and remedies"}, {"id": "afa83511-017d-4201-ad8f-ef3b226bbdab", "type": "concept", "title": "Objective memo, executive summary, oral briefing, source links, quotation discipline, and citation integrity"}], "description": "This subtopic develops concise reading and structured application rather than case-name memorization."}, {"id": "3fdda1ca-8c71-4b24-a33c-16ccf1ddef17", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dispute prevention and resolution", "children": [{"id": "e982243e-dc90-48c4-990e-f4fb6ef4fbb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Complaint handling, service recovery, reservation of rights, negotiation, demand letters, and without-prejudice concepts"}, {"id": "03907dd7-1b73-472a-910c-ad53dc583cdb", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediation, arbitration, class waivers, delegation, venue, governing law, administrative claims, and court litigation"}, {"id": "b8a49331-48d7-434b-b5da-b1b515b65123", "type": "concept", "title": "Settlement authority, releases, confidentiality, non-disparagement, regulatory reporting, enforcement, and post-dispute learning"}], "description": "Students compare process, cost, speed, privacy, precedent, enforceability, relationships, and fairness across resolution pathways."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$hlawjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'hospitality-law'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Hospitality Law',
  goal = 'Hospitality Law',
  summary = 'Hospitality Law prepares future hotel, restaurant, resort, club, and event leaders to recognize and manage legal risk in the United States. Students analyze contracts and agency, innkeeper–guest duties, torts and premises liability, safety and emergencies, food and alcohol regulation, employment and labor, accessibility and civil rights, franchising and management agreements, consumer protection, intellectual property, privacy and cybersecurity, insurance, compliance, investigations, and dispute resolution. Through cases, statutes, regulations, simulations, and professional writing, students learn to identify controlling authority, apply rules to facts, preserve evidence, communicate uncertainty, and escalate matters responsibly.',
  data = $hlawjson${"slug": "hospitality-law", "title": "Hospitality Law", "description": "Hospitality Law prepares future hotel, restaurant, resort, club, and event leaders to recognize and manage legal risk in the United States. Students analyze contracts and agency, innkeeper–guest duties, torts and premises liability, safety and emergencies, food and alcohol regulation, employment and labor, accessibility and civil rights, franchising and management agreements, consumer protection, intellectual property, privacy and cybersecurity, insurance, compliance, investigations, and dispute resolution. Through cases, statutes, regulations, simulations, and professional writing, students learn to identify controlling authority, apply rules to facts, preserve evidence, communicate uncertainty, and escalate matters responsibly.", "topics": [{"id": "b98462b1-1f6b-42c1-b23f-aac1d062a1cf", "type": "topic", "title": "The American Legal System and Hospitality Decision-Making", "description": "Hospitality managers operate where federal, state, tribal, territorial, and local rules overlap. This section builds the legal literacy needed to recognize an issue, find controlling authority, preserve facts, and involve qualified counsel before an operational problem becomes a claim.", "children": [{"id": "8271beca-2277-405d-ad50-d23c9f858981", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sources and hierarchy of law", "children": [{"id": "ea686003-2054-4448-aa5e-66726fda3139", "type": "concept", "title": "U.S. Constitution; federal and state constitutions"}, {"id": "bf84affe-a4ec-463c-be28-dd488d45b328", "type": "concept", "title": "Statutes, regulations, ordinances, administrative guidance, and licensing conditions"}, {"id": "179f3391-803a-43fe-8c09-63e7b2217154", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal and state judicial opinions; binding precedent versus persuasive authority"}], "description": "Students learn which legal authority controls, how conflicts are resolved, and why an online summary is not a substitute for current primary law."}, {"id": "15e233d9-2de9-4c36-998b-5c513307203d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Courts, agencies, jurisdiction, and procedure", "children": [{"id": "539fa714-b222-47b8-a211-657ad8ea9618", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal and state trial and appellate courts; subject-matter and personal jurisdiction"}, {"id": "52a766fa-c3bd-4438-81b0-f84d857e0c84", "type": "concept", "title": "Administrative agencies, investigations, inspections, hearings, penalties, and judicial review"}, {"id": "bf51ed3b-8e9d-4f98-92d8-cc89d327f7f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Pleadings, discovery, motions, trial, appeals, burdens of proof, remedies, and limitation periods"}], "description": "This subtopic maps the institutions that create, enforce, and interpret hospitality obligations."}, {"id": "6f3a04b4-5897-45f3-b85f-fecedeb1274c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Managerial issue spotting and escalation", "children": [{"id": "56b37582-e457-4a1f-92c6-5af700152070", "type": "concept", "title": "Parties, duties, conduct, causation, injury, defenses, damages, and available remedies"}, {"id": "bbe599f0-b38e-4486-851b-371d325e0c04", "type": "concept", "title": "Privilege, litigation holds, records preservation, incident reports, and communications discipline"}, {"id": "42fd5f2b-5e58-4159-914d-a846f8e9249e", "type": "concept", "title": "Counsel referral, insurer notice, regulator response, expert consultation, and decision documentation"}], "description": "Students practice turning an operational story into legally relevant facts, questions, evidence, and decisions without pretending to provide legal advice."}]}, {"id": "30bfa9b3-db9e-423b-a01d-e489ee9267c1", "type": "topic", "title": "Contracts, Agency, and Commercial Commitments", "description": "Hospitality operations are built on promises to guests, groups, suppliers, owners, brands, platforms, and employees. Students learn how agreements form, who may bind the enterprise, and how contract language allocates operational and financial risk.", "children": [{"id": "8c73ef71-a2ab-4d9c-ad3e-4ada85ea46ad", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Formation, interpretation, and enforceability", "children": [{"id": "c280d2e8-48fe-4007-85f3-18c12d4742f0", "type": "concept", "title": "Offer, acceptance, consideration, mutual assent, capacity, legality, and definite terms"}, {"id": "c5064a15-8c29-4c99-84a4-a0c3cc534048", "type": "concept", "title": "Written, oral, electronic, clickwrap, course-of-dealing, and implied agreements"}, {"id": "bbc61f6a-a34b-447e-8da8-4857c23a9b13", "type": "concept", "title": "Statute of Frauds, parol evidence, ambiguity, modification, waiver, severability, and electronic signatures"}], "description": "Students learn the elements of a contract and the recurring defects that make an apparent promise uncertain or unenforceable."}, {"id": "8715bfad-d1fe-46f6-920d-bf8c0288232e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Performance, breach, defenses, and remedies", "children": [{"id": "1f6e43e6-73ad-4a49-a6d0-434a24236f34", "type": "concept", "title": "Conditions, covenants, representations, warranties, standards, milestones, and acceptance"}, {"id": "c3cf1b13-33f2-4df9-8cac-f458ff54ad75", "type": "concept", "title": "Material breach, anticipatory repudiation, impossibility, impracticability, frustration, mistake, duress, and unconscionability"}, {"id": "752950be-af47-454b-9b23-87935d64eb09", "type": "concept", "title": "Expectation, reliance, restitution, liquidated damages, mitigation, specific performance, termination, and cure"}], "description": "This subtopic connects contract doctrine to cancellations, service failures, payment disputes, and disrupted events."}, {"id": "9dbf02b0-124d-49f6-bae6-20ae3ecf86cf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Agency and authority", "children": [{"id": "1e3b99e3-7830-4c2c-9c89-6e3abca49e76", "type": "concept", "title": "Actual, implied, apparent, and ratified authority"}, {"id": "41798752-1f2e-4c27-ad2f-cc4bf4bf09ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Principal and agent duties; disclosed, partially disclosed, and undisclosed principals"}, {"id": "851d055e-0e6e-4666-afcf-a61d5aae1ca1", "type": "concept", "title": "Vicarious liability, independent contractors, scope of employment, and authority controls"}], "description": "Students examine when employees, managers, agents, travel sellers, and platforms create obligations for another party."}]}, {"id": "b3d97d1f-13a6-4591-b075-f89afc76f5cd", "type": "topic", "title": "Innkeeper–Guest Relationship, Reservations, and Guest Property", "description": "Lodging law combines common-law duties, state innkeeper statutes, contracts, civil-rights rules, and consumer protections. Students learn how legal status changes from inquiry and reservation through occupancy, removal, departure, and lost-property handling.", "children": [{"id": "bbcc3975-a826-4075-846f-d65342aeebde", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Admission, reservations, rates, and nondiscrimination", "children": [{"id": "003fdbbd-d338-4acb-bda0-fe4942c8cbca", "type": "concept", "title": "Guest status, right to exclude, lawful refusal, protected classes, and neutral conduct rules"}, {"id": "7d0841d6-ec67-4e7d-93e2-40be19de67f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Reservation confirmation, deposits, guarantees, cancellations, no-shows, overbooking, and walking guests"}, {"id": "2f697650-428c-4794-8516-452b767f71af", "type": "concept", "title": "Rate disclosure, mandatory fees, taxes, authorization holds, refunds, and records"}], "description": "Students evaluate when a lodging operator may refuse service, what reservation promises mean, and how published terms must align with public-accommodation duties."}, {"id": "a9ba849a-4acb-4b18-aac1-c537604e74e4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Occupancy, privacy, access, and removal", "children": [{"id": "b9e49176-2c83-4ae3-ad9a-4e5555d53d07", "type": "concept", "title": "Guest privacy, room entry, housekeeping, maintenance, emergencies, warrants, subpoenas, and law-enforcement requests"}, {"id": "ed8a237c-21ec-4cc6-8c3c-702017735acd", "type": "concept", "title": "Distinguishing guest, tenant, licensee, trespasser, and long-term occupant under state law"}, {"id": "ad108c33-bffd-411d-a6ab-8f2d6bc4c2c5", "type": "concept", "title": "Eviction or ejection, breach of peace, abandoned rooms, safe procedures, and counsel/law-enforcement escalation"}], "description": "This subtopic addresses the guest's possessory and privacy interests and the operator's safety and property-management responsibilities."}, {"id": "97e8175d-2180-4ae0-a605-5dd40cedc17b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Bailment, safekeeping, lost property, and statutory limits", "children": [{"id": "25d8fba6-aca0-4848-aa72-c425fa9257e2", "type": "concept", "title": "Bailment formation, standard of care, proof, defenses, and damages"}, {"id": "68bc96a6-55ca-4413-ba07-8cee8282682b", "type": "concept", "title": "Innkeeper statutes, safe-deposit procedures, posted notices, parking disclaimers, and limits of liability"}, {"id": "7e7d9747-f7d6-4275-be3b-7cdf4c50075d", "type": "concept", "title": "Lost-and-found chain of custody, retention, disposal, employee property, and evidence preservation"}], "description": "Students learn how custody and notice affect responsibility for luggage, vehicles, valuables, and property left behind."}]}, {"id": "43eaa9a2-8b47-4561-97ff-16ec3e99d148", "type": "topic", "title": "Torts, Negligence, and Premises Liability", "description": "Hospitality businesses invite the public into spaces containing foreseeable service, crowd, pool, elevator, food, alcohol, and security risks. This section teaches a disciplined negligence analysis and the operational evidence needed to prevent or defend claims.", "children": [{"id": "c0bd69e1-ddcb-4184-9db3-630151d0d647", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intentional torts and business responsibility", "children": [{"id": "a4355494-5ba7-4da4-8c59-3e12880d7378", "type": "concept", "title": "Assault, battery, false imprisonment, trespass, conversion, defamation, privacy torts, and intentional infliction"}, {"id": "0ab82a45-a0d4-4e34-9bf7-ed23eb362693", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent, privilege, self-defense, defense of others or property, merchant detention, and use of force"}, {"id": "9929109c-b569-4c37-a856-b60b111b6aed", "type": "concept", "title": "Respondeat superior, negligent hiring/supervision/retention, ratification, and punitive damages"}], "description": "Students distinguish intentional conduct from negligence and identify when an employer may be liable for employee or security actions."}, {"id": "d9f2dae7-b1f9-44c9-ba0c-d1e809e8301e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Negligence framework", "children": [{"id": "ca09139e-9463-4055-9830-019f578724d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Reasonable care, industry custom, statutes and negligence per se, professional standards, and foreseeable plaintiffs"}, {"id": "76264dae-edd6-44d5-bf6b-599a6791949a", "type": "concept", "title": "Actual and proximate causation, intervening acts, multiple causes, and proof"}, {"id": "fb958941-89c9-43b5-97bb-676e0cf07e07", "type": "concept", "title": "Compensatory damages, comparative or contributory fault, assumption of risk, waivers, and indemnity"}], "description": "This subtopic builds the core method for analyzing duty, breach, causation, injury, and defenses."}, {"id": "8f7062f8-37af-46ca-b6f6-be7283c62c4c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Premises, products, and third-party acts", "children": [{"id": "3458fbd1-a2da-49f9-bdae-b0707052b27e", "type": "concept", "title": "Inspection, notice, maintenance, warnings, lighting, flooring, stairs, balconies, pools, spas, elevators, and parking"}, {"id": "0caf9b94-fa4a-40c2-88e1-a44712727685", "type": "concept", "title": "Invitees, licensees, trespassers, children, recreational activities, and jurisdictional variations"}, {"id": "c3d8bc19-9d40-4783-a505-2fb8b979c8cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Foreseeable crime, security plans, keys and locks, vendors, products liability, recalls, and evidence"}], "description": "Students apply negligence doctrine to physical conditions, products, vendors, criminal acts, and changing property use."}]}, {"id": "e93a57c0-6677-47e0-bf8a-cfbb5f8b24a2", "type": "topic", "title": "Safety, Security, Emergencies, and Public-Health Duties", "description": "Hospitality managers must make rapid decisions during fires, severe weather, violence, medical events, outbreaks, evacuations, and technology outages. This section connects duty of care to preparedness, response, continuity, documentation, and respectful communication.", "children": [{"id": "15ed900b-8310-4670-9c5a-3b315b6f64a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Emergency planning and duty of care", "children": [{"id": "35767f7c-1d81-4bde-9a36-27f5be4c30ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Hazard assessment, emergency action plans, evacuation, shelter, accountability, reunification, and continuity"}, {"id": "d8b5b3b2-ccae-4f66-b52f-58d84f58c6e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Fire and life safety, occupancy, alarms, suppression, exits, crowd management, pools, and transportation"}, {"id": "18765760-88f7-41dd-9ece-ed30f4c0c667", "type": "concept", "title": "Emergency roles, incident command, drills, mutual aid, contractors, and accessible communications"}], "description": "Students learn to design a proportionate all-hazards program and understand that plans must align with local codes and public-safety authorities."}, {"id": "f2c2577b-a6f5-4c7b-8c7b-7362d75ee247", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Security, violence, and safeguarding", "children": [{"id": "87b83b39-1d91-42fe-baac-e450846d5cf8", "type": "concept", "title": "Threat assessment, access control, keys, surveillance, patrol, cash, cyber-physical security, and suspicious activity"}, {"id": "b1aeaec7-2585-48c9-9dec-6234b0c7bd0c", "type": "concept", "title": "Workplace violence, trafficking indicators, vulnerable guests, minors, harassment, and escalation protocols"}, {"id": "48c9ffbb-0b14-4a26-87c2-1ef088b6558f", "type": "concept", "title": "Security contractors, off-duty police, use of force, privacy, records, and post-incident care"}], "description": "This subtopic examines reasonable protective measures without assuming that every adverse event is preventable."}, {"id": "8f08e384-780b-4ebf-9750-c904d00e73fe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Medical events, outbreaks, and government orders", "children": [{"id": "0ac77327-46fd-4889-92c2-4815a7426dda", "type": "concept", "title": "First aid/AED programs, emergency medical services, Good Samaritan variation, and documentation"}, {"id": "c7723342-afbb-4dcc-a2a0-27056b479317", "type": "concept", "title": "Communicable disease, exposure, isolation, sanitation, closures, public-health orders, and worker protections"}, {"id": "b9ca7d8a-affc-4c43-98b8-200bfdb0708b", "type": "concept", "title": "Americans with Disabilities Act issues, confidentiality, rumor control, media response, and recovery"}], "description": "Students practice coordinating guest care, employee safety, operations, privacy, and agency direction during health events."}]}, {"id": "3fa82243-5fa0-462c-a233-bb1fbfa95326", "type": "topic", "title": "Food Safety, Allergens, and Alcohol Regulation", "description": "Restaurants, bars, banquets, and lodging outlets face layered state and local licensing, food-code, alcohol, and tort obligations. Students learn to translate regulatory duties into preventive controls and defensible records.", "children": [{"id": "047cca9a-4e87-4f95-bbce-003556e9a419", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Retail food regulation and active managerial control", "children": [{"id": "e58a4bb8-9683-4c38-919a-74daab13a26e", "type": "concept", "title": "Food establishment permits, inspections, grades, embargo, correction, closure, hearings, and appeals"}, {"id": "cc66cf36-5ae8-43ac-a81f-139430b6701b", "type": "concept", "title": "Person in charge, employee health, hygiene, time/temperature control, contamination, sanitation, HACCP, and variances"}, {"id": "6801fc20-68fa-4248-b453-382ad5f3ba81", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier approval, traceability, recalls, complaints, outbreak cooperation, logs, and corrective action"}], "description": "Students learn how the FDA Food Code functions as a model and why the adopted state or local code and permit conditions control the operation."}, {"id": "9cf1cf7a-18cb-4bef-83ec-c4364c255904", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Food allergens and consumer communication", "children": [{"id": "17dfba8d-844c-4f3a-b0e1-b4738aa72265", "type": "concept", "title": "Nine major allergens under federal packaged-food law; jurisdiction-specific restaurant requirements"}, {"id": "e6a2b4d2-70e7-4047-8b14-151693154e27", "type": "concept", "title": "Written allergen notification under jurisdictions adopting relevant FDA Food Code provisions"}, {"id": "08a4e6f3-9009-4b9b-b269-62b8e0166144", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-contact prevention, recipe control, substitutions, server escalation, emergency response, and documentation"}], "description": "This subtopic addresses the legal and operational consequences of inaccurate ingredient, menu, and service communication."}, {"id": "32bbd449-13a0-4d8d-9b6a-7d3c5d4c8cb6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Alcohol licensing and liability", "children": [{"id": "8f2e97f6-96f1-4672-85f8-f71419e93b9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Licenses, permits, tied-house and supplier issues, hours, age verification, records, and enforcement"}, {"id": "1e2aed1a-9a6c-4181-9b12-2474a2617986", "type": "concept", "title": "Responsible service, intoxication, underage service, promotions, delivery, cannabis interactions, and refusal"}, {"id": "cb1bceb3-f1a6-412f-ae01-11191c1c1862", "type": "concept", "title": "Dram-shop and social-host liability, causation, safe transportation, incident reporting, and insurance"}], "description": "Students compare the three-tier system and state/local rules while recognizing that service, age, hours, promotions, and liability vary substantially by jurisdiction."}]}, {"id": "6ff36760-bd3b-410d-b2d8-cabc181e62ed", "type": "topic", "title": "Employment, Wage-and-Hour, Labor, and Immigration Compliance", "description": "Hospitality's round-the-clock, tipped, multilingual, seasonal, and franchise-based workforce creates distinctive legal risk. This section helps future managers apply fair, documented practices and recognize when federal, state, local, union, or immigration rules require specialist support.", "children": [{"id": "ca731f04-99e0-41f5-9d03-3de4dd68df79", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Wage-and-hour and scheduling", "children": [{"id": "6014f98e-04df-49f6-a0c6-3c709adbbbf1", "type": "concept", "title": "FLSA coverage, employee versus contractor, exempt versus nonexempt, hours worked, regular rate, overtime, and records"}, {"id": "2750b638-7e8e-4279-b8a9-481b9d958906", "type": "concept", "title": "Tip credit, notice, tip pools, managers and tips, service charges, dual jobs, shortages, uniforms, and lodging/meal credits"}, {"id": "b72b6d63-9051-4b32-aaf4-1771da897f60", "type": "concept", "title": "State/local minimum wages, predictive scheduling, meal/rest periods, pay frequency, final pay, expense reimbursement, and paid leave"}], "description": "Students examine the records and classification decisions behind wages, tips, overtime, deductions, meals, uniforms, and working time."}, {"id": "83354034-6257-4892-aa44-3a3b3c0fae22", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Equal employment opportunity and accommodation", "children": [{"id": "4c2fcb7a-a3e6-4bd1-b4d2-82ba42f6f2b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Title VII, ADA, ADEA, Equal Pay Act, GINA, Pregnancy Workers Fairness Act, and state/local protections"}, {"id": "6e31849c-da28-431f-bd17-48bb196b3531", "type": "concept", "title": "Disability, religion, pregnancy, lactation, interactive process, undue hardship, confidentiality, and retaliation"}, {"id": "a035349a-9ba1-426a-b40f-1aa341f1584f", "type": "concept", "title": "Harassment by supervisors, coworkers, guests, vendors, and digital channels; reporting, investigation, and corrective action"}], "description": "This subtopic covers nondiscrimination across recruitment, assignment, pay, promotion, discipline, harassment prevention, accommodation, and separation."}, {"id": "832c2251-4f00-4b1a-a932-8cc31401b731", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Labor relations, leave, safety, and work authorization", "children": [{"id": "c6446d4c-2ae8-40e5-9c89-caf2f7cb077b", "type": "concept", "title": "NLRA protected concerted activity, wage discussions, organizing, supervisors, union rules, bargaining, and discipline"}, {"id": "af0adace-7ab5-4d6c-8fc2-069c7bff6b10", "type": "concept", "title": "OSHA duties, hazard communication, injury records, workers' compensation, FMLA, USERRA, and state leave laws"}, {"id": "0353ae7c-eca1-49e8-a266-d29e400b9477", "type": "concept", "title": "Form I-9, nondiscriminatory verification, E-Verify where applicable, visas, minors, trafficking risks, and document retention"}], "description": "Students learn the overlapping rights that affect employee voice, injury prevention, leave, organizing, and verification."}]}, {"id": "4e02811c-dbb9-42cc-b27d-9aab10d09df5", "type": "topic", "title": "Accessibility and Civil Rights in Guest Service", "description": "American hospitality is a public-accommodation setting. Students learn to design equal access across reservations, facilities, transportation, digital channels, communication, policies, and emergency procedures—not merely react to complaints.", "children": [{"id": "fa9b3d53-eabe-4ca6-909d-50b3b5a0cab1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ADA Title III service obligations", "children": [{"id": "6f1cc06a-451e-43e5-a863-4bf8a616ac6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Public accommodations, eligibility criteria, surcharges, direct threat, fundamental alteration, and undue burden"}, {"id": "952ed21b-95a2-4796-9ce5-824deb01f04e", "type": "concept", "title": "Service animals, mobility devices, auxiliary aids, interpreters, captioning, accessible formats, and companions"}, {"id": "449f907b-f6ff-4406-b25a-c1372bccaa13", "type": "concept", "title": "Reservation staff knowledge, accessible-room information, room holds, equivalent options, and training"}], "description": "Students apply the concepts of equal enjoyment, reasonable policy modification, effective communication, and barrier removal to real hospitality interactions."}, {"id": "cb7ee80f-1274-4098-b8f4-f15bfcf1b976", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Facilities, alterations, and operational access", "children": [{"id": "980df0ba-90b5-4d83-aafa-c37afbdd16a8", "type": "concept", "title": "2010 ADA Standards, new construction, alterations, path of travel, barrier removal, and readily achievable analysis"}, {"id": "f899dd81-07c9-4242-955b-d1629eb618b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Entrances, parking, counters, guest rooms, bathrooms, pools, restaurants, meeting rooms, fitness, transportation, and evacuation"}, {"id": "2801f129-856c-46d3-900e-a275f17c0592", "type": "concept", "title": "Maintenance of accessible features, temporary barriers, furniture, snow, outages, inspections, and remediation"}], "description": "This subtopic links design standards with daily practices that keep accessible features usable."}, {"id": "aca43de3-99be-45f6-be02-7cd5247ed980", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital access and broader civil-rights duties", "children": [{"id": "852e46e3-c565-4be2-a91c-bbbd9fbb3aff", "type": "concept", "title": "Booking, menus, check-in, digital keys, loyalty, employment portals, documents, and effective alternatives"}, {"id": "a3fe1bd4-3a54-4129-97fc-7132f4832dbf", "type": "concept", "title": "DOJ web-accessibility guidance, WCAG as a technical reference, procurement, testing, complaints, and remediation"}, {"id": "5e14bb65-1eb8-4684-89ae-d7f0a11cf077", "type": "concept", "title": "Race, color, religion, national origin, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability, and other state/local protected classes"}], "description": "Students examine websites, apps, kiosks, and the interaction of federal law with state and local public-accommodation protections."}]}, {"id": "4656b6b5-1367-43ed-8b30-3b1b2d6e494c", "type": "topic", "title": "Ownership, Franchising, Management Agreements, and Real Estate", "description": "Hospitality assets often separate ownership, brand, operation, employment, real estate, and intellectual property. This section helps students identify who controls which decision and where obligations, fees, standards, and liability reside.", "children": [{"id": "4e63b7fc-61fb-4368-ac7c-f39e2729828c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Entity, ownership, and authority structures", "children": [{"id": "59567bdb-d64a-41f0-a108-9459424b5daf", "type": "concept", "title": "Corporations, limited liability companies, partnerships, joint ventures, owners, operators, brands, and asset managers"}, {"id": "5cc0b336-b258-4909-acfa-df364952cb47", "type": "concept", "title": "Governing documents, fiduciary duties, authority matrices, guarantees, indemnities, and intercompany agreements"}, {"id": "9690d7d1-b8b2-4067-9bb0-ba3707c333e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Bankruptcy, receivership, lender rights, change of control, due diligence, and successor exposure"}], "description": "Students map legal entities and decision rights before attributing a promise, duty, asset, employee, or claim to the wrong party."}, {"id": "2ea33f7c-f1be-48ee-973e-fa9c2692c00f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Franchise relationships", "children": [{"id": "e267a8a9-a871-41c7-b163-e5d2b0feb421", "type": "concept", "title": "FTC Franchise Rule, Franchise Disclosure Document, 23 disclosure items, timing, and earnings claims"}, {"id": "a13d6835-e72c-4675-8810-22588f5b577a", "type": "concept", "title": "Brand standards, fees, reservations, loyalty, procurement, technology, territory, quality assurance, defaults, cure, and termination"}, {"id": "67ba5c9b-580f-44ac-b687-0ff520a90a39", "type": "concept", "title": "State registration and relationship laws, encroachment, good faith, vicarious liability, and joint-employer concerns"}], "description": "This subtopic introduces federal disclosure rules and the contract and state-law issues that shape hotel and restaurant franchises."}, {"id": "9fe1925a-de78-4232-bf84-117b6176eca5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Hotel management and property agreements", "children": [{"id": "ede4fbc7-bde5-4445-8a46-614c525400c8", "type": "concept", "title": "Owner/operator roles, term, base and incentive fees, budget, personnel, accounts, procurement, and performance tests"}, {"id": "010301a9-66c6-4e08-be64-e790d184836c", "type": "concept", "title": "Licenses, leases, easements, zoning, permits, land use, environmental conditions, and nuisance"}, {"id": "3a781cc6-a334-4771-81f6-5811654f4deb", "type": "concept", "title": "Capital plans, insurance, indemnity, condemnation, casualty, force majeure, termination, and transition"}], "description": "Students compare management contracts and real-estate arrangements that determine control, economics, standards, and exit rights."}]}, {"id": "a2a659df-7e31-4fce-afa6-929a99b6bd91", "type": "topic", "title": "Consumer Protection, Marketing, Pricing, and Intellectual Property", "description": "Hospitality representations appear in rates, fees, menus, reviews, loyalty terms, photos, music, events, and influencer content. Students learn to assess what a reasonable consumer is likely to understand and whether the business can substantiate its claims and rights.", "children": [{"id": "7f921f53-d792-448e-b746-b44b59a6642e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Pricing, fees, promotions, and unfair practices", "children": [{"id": "c5c457b7-f09d-45a6-be59-359ba15bd616", "type": "concept", "title": "Total price disclosure for covered short-term lodging, mandatory fees, optional add-ons, taxes, clear and conspicuous presentation"}, {"id": "9f49a848-91ae-437d-8a4f-b2893cbc2615", "type": "concept", "title": "Coupons, packages, deposits, refunds, cancellation, scarcity claims, loyalty prices, gift cards, and automatic renewal"}, {"id": "091d2669-dedb-4e4e-a090-e53817d69da1", "type": "concept", "title": "Unfair or deceptive acts, state UDAP laws, attorney-general enforcement, private claims, class actions, and records"}], "description": "Students connect the FTC Act, the federal rule on unfair or deceptive fees, and state consumer-protection law to the guest purchase journey."}, {"id": "23f41b5f-aa0c-4c11-9666-ac560b397a2e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advertising, reviews, and endorsements", "children": [{"id": "ab66e8d2-a7bb-4886-a34c-f1a7fbcd2227", "type": "concept", "title": "Claim substantiation, disclosures, photos, amenities, accessibility, sustainability, health, safety, and comparative claims"}, {"id": "a3c5b487-7b0c-4af2-b965-0a3f6c9cbb5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Influencers, employees, affiliates, travel advisors, native advertising, endorsements, and material connections"}, {"id": "a072d141-2a52-4a3d-94c2-2b9278044d53", "type": "concept", "title": "Consumer reviews, fake reviews, suppression, incentives, platform terms, reputation management, and defamation risk"}], "description": "This subtopic focuses on truthful claims, material connections, review integrity, and consistency across direct and intermediary channels."}, {"id": "bedba8c0-dd76-44b9-a82d-3783adcc1837", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Intellectual property and publicity", "children": [{"id": "0ca3f8e9-6776-4423-9dea-ace30c0920c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Trademarks, trade dress, domain names, licenses, franchised marks, quality control, and infringement"}, {"id": "4c3b9aac-7697-4331-befc-6aebaefe8d2e", "type": "concept", "title": "Copyright in photos, menus, websites, software, music, video, décor, training, and user-generated content"}, {"id": "16e407b8-de15-43b8-aa9d-64f3268f86ab", "type": "concept", "title": "Patents, trade secrets, confidentiality, employee work, rights of publicity, releases, and takedowns"}], "description": "Students identify the permissions needed to use brands, creative works, performances, guest images, and event content."}]}, {"id": "7ab33aaa-3d8d-498f-926b-5e188a270132", "type": "topic", "title": "Privacy, Data Security, Surveillance, and Technology Law", "description": "Hospitality businesses collect identity, payment, location, preference, loyalty, employment, and sometimes biometric data. Students learn to map the data life cycle, honor representations, reduce unnecessary collection, and prepare for incidents across a patchwork of U.S. laws.", "children": [{"id": "2ef4cd43-5c5d-41f7-90b0-efb88cac6fab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Privacy governance and consumer rights", "children": [{"id": "35b0a4a9-ec19-4468-b658-6a1a9ab6d44d", "type": "concept", "title": "Data inventory, classification, purpose, minimization, notice, consent, access, correction, deletion, retention, disposal, and accountability"}, {"id": "7768125b-89dd-4a78-985f-7cf1295fd2d7", "type": "concept", "title": "State comprehensive privacy laws, biometric and facial-recognition laws, children's data, marketing communications, cookies, and location"}, {"id": "2005714d-98f1-425d-b5e6-e6f59650ef1c", "type": "concept", "title": "Service providers, data sales/sharing, cross-border transfers, loyalty programs, sensitive data, and dark patterns"}], "description": "Students examine what data is collected, why, under which notice or permission, and which jurisdiction or contract governs it."}, {"id": "4e411651-7907-4e18-af6c-3d5a70523fd7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reasonable security and vendor risk", "children": [{"id": "9180786d-0431-4340-ab8b-0153567ecc91", "type": "concept", "title": "FTC Act, state security statutes, PCI DSS as a contractual standard, incident representations, and industry practice"}, {"id": "ab67c825-d5a0-469c-9843-4f6e95f085a9", "type": "concept", "title": "Access control, multifactor authentication, encryption, patching, logging, backups, physical security, training, and testing"}, {"id": "bcee648b-f1d0-44d1-8e40-a283f57433b9", "type": "concept", "title": "Cloud, PMS/POS, franchise, platform, payment, Wi-Fi, IoT, vendor diligence, security clauses, audit, and termination"}], "description": "This subtopic translates legal expectations and contractual duties into governance and operational safeguards."}, {"id": "0231897d-50b8-4e9c-b9d3-009dad50f1f3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Surveillance, incident response, and breach notice", "children": [{"id": "a51e4c08-22dd-43fc-89e6-0ad19102b493", "type": "concept", "title": "Cameras, audio, key logs, Wi-Fi analytics, location, biometrics, employee monitoring, notices, and restricted areas"}, {"id": "8f17f9d5-0b45-4d20-9760-e67b9d3c1848", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident triage, containment, privilege, forensics, insurer, law enforcement, regulators, payment brands, and communications"}, {"id": "bb0deaa9-01ca-4ca5-bd24-515462eb7f1b", "type": "concept", "title": "State breach-notification triggers, timing, affected individuals, content, regulator/consumer-reporting notices, remediation, and lessons"}], "description": "Students balance safety and analytics with privacy, labor, discrimination, and evidence concerns."}]}, {"id": "dcb40b03-3abb-47f8-ac6d-52f37475c651", "type": "topic", "title": "Risk Management, Insurance, Indemnity, and Claims", "description": "Legal risk cannot be eliminated, but it can be allocated, financed, monitored, and reduced. This section connects contracts and insurance with operational controls, reporting discipline, and fair treatment of injured or affected people.", "children": [{"id": "0889a7ed-73ff-4ce3-8706-baed82076977", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Enterprise and operational risk assessment", "children": [{"id": "5b2ff728-c097-40c8-a49f-230f576fa662", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk registers, frequency, severity, velocity, aggregation, emerging risk, and risk appetite"}, {"id": "5895fc53-4f1c-4064-801b-e787e99324e5", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoid, reduce, transfer, finance, accept, monitor, and escalate"}, {"id": "7e6a1816-2d49-4726-9805-b9a6463ce63b", "type": "concept", "title": "Policies, training, inspections, maintenance, audits, complaints, near misses, corrective action, and board reporting"}], "description": "Students use a repeatable process to identify hazards, affected parties, controls, owners, evidence, and residual risk."}, {"id": "d86d0cef-b507-48f5-aee2-5540425cea92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Insurance and contractual allocation", "children": [{"id": "09c260b5-e6ec-43f2-8f95-924351a706a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Commercial general liability, property, business interruption, cyber, crime, auto, liquor, employment practices, workers' compensation, and umbrella"}, {"id": "235ef4e8-ed3f-43db-b805-e3ac0ff41b09", "type": "concept", "title": "Named insured, additional insured, occurrence, claims-made, limits, retentions, deductibles, exclusions, endorsements, and certificates"}, {"id": "25f6b966-4ab8-4b8f-b0b8-6422a3018e26", "type": "concept", "title": "Indemnity, defense, limitation of liability, waiver of subrogation, insurance requirements, and anti-indemnity variation"}], "description": "This subtopic helps managers recognize common coverage structures and contract language requiring broker or counsel review."}, {"id": "b8a6fb4e-100d-496d-b72e-ff4b983b639d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Incident, claim, and litigation readiness", "children": [{"id": "1c81d629-36a9-45c2-b4f9-04500f94f72d", "type": "concept", "title": "Immediate care, scene safety, photographs, witnesses, video retention, products, logs, and chain of custody"}, {"id": "54bf3d4e-6804-44e8-b433-1a2d14397838", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident reports, privilege, insurer notice, reservation of rights, adjusters, experts, subpoenas, and litigation holds"}, {"id": "74977cf2-6c08-489d-ac4e-9a76605ae372", "type": "concept", "title": "Root-cause analysis, remedial measures, regulator cooperation, settlement authority, and lessons learned"}], "description": "Students practice a compassionate and evidence-preserving response that avoids admissions, retaliation, spoliation, and late notice."}]}, {"id": "a4eb286f-37d7-4b41-bc12-2389acbd0930", "type": "topic", "title": "Compliance Programs, Ethics, Investigations, and Governance", "description": "A policy manual alone is not a compliance system. Students learn to build governance that assigns ownership, makes reporting safe, verifies controls, corrects problems, and connects legal duties with hospitality ethics and stakeholder trust.", "children": [{"id": "d0206957-9fbe-4cf3-a5f2-4deed9faf804", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Compliance program design", "children": [{"id": "51f61eac-077c-49f5-ad28-185570c252e0", "type": "concept", "title": "Risk assessment, obligations register, policies, standards, procedures, controls, owners, and evidence"}, {"id": "1251f8f3-af23-4831-b827-85ad1d8560a1", "type": "concept", "title": "Training, communications, certifications, monitoring, testing, audits, hotline, and third-party management"}, {"id": "564a4fa2-7df6-4b30-bde3-bf6b9cead052", "type": "concept", "title": "Metrics, exceptions, remediation, discipline, incentives, reporting, and continuous improvement"}], "description": "Students convert a legal inventory into practical controls and assurance activities suited to a property or enterprise."}, {"id": "42db401a-87c4-4f19-98b1-75a59b083238", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Complaints and workplace investigations", "children": [{"id": "5dad091a-c08b-4b4b-842a-0c67f9c173f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Intake, triage, conflicts, interim measures, scope, plan, witnesses, documents, interviews, and credibility"}, {"id": "c32363c5-715c-43d9-b231-badda3d640f7", "type": "concept", "title": "Need-to-know confidentiality, privilege decisions, trauma-informed practice, accommodations, translation, and records"}, {"id": "09b39104-7bcb-48ce-a89d-df39f794355e", "type": "concept", "title": "Findings, standard of proof, corrective action, communication, anti-retaliation monitoring, and appeal or review"}], "description": "This subtopic emphasizes fair, prompt, confidential-to-the-extent-possible processes that protect evidence and prohibit retaliation."}, {"id": "557128d3-528d-4e98-8c48-200d044e5c19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Ethical judgment and governance", "children": [{"id": "989c0aca-e7ff-43b9-893f-c1601dd1820b", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflicts of interest, gifts, bribery, procurement integrity, accurate books, whistleblowing, and board oversight"}, {"id": "8c9ec961-ff43-447c-ae65-c6717fea0ec2", "type": "concept", "title": "Guest dignity, worker voice, vulnerable people, environmental impacts, community relations, and human rights"}, {"id": "6c58dc44-ae32-45c1-a033-3d5a50adea60", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethical frameworks, stakeholder mapping, escalation, dissent, documentation, accountability, and learning culture"}], "description": "Students analyze what responsible hospitality leadership requires when legal minimums, commercial pressure, and stakeholder interests diverge."}]}, {"id": "c1aba699-f1de-435e-90cb-674388050c83", "type": "topic", "title": "Legal Research, Case Briefing, Dispute Resolution, and Advocacy", "description": "The course culminates in the ability to read law carefully, separate rule from commentary, apply authority to facts, and communicate a defensible recommendation. Students also evaluate when negotiation, mediation, arbitration, agency process, or litigation best serves the organization and affected stakeholders.", "children": [{"id": "31d9b7e3-fae3-4c8a-bd08-7244b8e7aa6a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Research and authority validation", "children": [{"id": "1bd5a79e-08b9-45b4-8dcb-58e646f559c7", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue statements, search terms, secondary orientation, primary authority, citators, and updating"}, {"id": "cda5a40d-718f-4990-bb23-d345f10019af", "type": "concept", "title": "Statutory and regulatory definitions, scope, exemptions, preemption, effective dates, amendments, and agency materials"}, {"id": "1ed27603-9b50-476c-8b32-dc91140f17e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Federal, state, tribal, territorial, and local sources; court rules; licenses; permits; contracts; and recordkeeping"}], "description": "Students learn a reproducible method for finding current law and confirming that it applies to the relevant place, date, facts, and business."}, {"id": "52796484-572b-4329-83f1-198534bff6a4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case briefing and legal analysis", "children": [{"id": "9da3a3a5-a226-49bd-bca7-824ef2e14d5c", "type": "concept", "title": "Citation, court, procedural posture, legally significant facts, issue, rule, holding, reasoning, disposition, and separate opinions"}, {"id": "4a397e63-a618-45e9-b5ab-a9260abfeaca", "type": "concept", "title": "IRAC/CREAC, analogies and distinctions, counterarguments, uncertainty, policy, and remedies"}, {"id": "afa83511-017d-4201-ad8f-ef3b226bbdab", "type": "concept", "title": "Objective memo, executive summary, oral briefing, source links, quotation discipline, and citation integrity"}], "description": "This subtopic develops concise reading and structured application rather than case-name memorization."}, {"id": "3fdda1ca-8c71-4b24-a33c-16ccf1ddef17", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Dispute prevention and resolution", "children": [{"id": "e982243e-dc90-48c4-990e-f4fb6ef4fbb5", "type": "concept", "title": "Complaint handling, service recovery, reservation of rights, negotiation, demand letters, and without-prejudice concepts"}, {"id": "03907dd7-1b73-472a-910c-ad53dc583cdb", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediation, arbitration, class waivers, delegation, venue, governing law, administrative claims, and court litigation"}, {"id": "b8a49331-48d7-434b-b5da-b1b515b65123", "type": "concept", "title": "Settlement authority, releases, confidentiality, non-disparagement, regulatory reporting, enforcement, and post-dispute learning"}], "description": "Students compare process, cost, speed, privacy, precedent, enforceability, relationships, and fairness across resolution pathways."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$hlawjson$::jsonb,
